# Loading ingested problems

Import ProblemRecord from "./problem_record.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import OpdpProfile from "./opdp_profile.lg".
Import LoadRules from "./load_rules.lg".

The ingest roles write what a source holds as lines of JSON: `problems.jsonl`
(one `Problem` a line), `nodes.jsonl` (the graph, parents first) and, for the
OPDP atlas, `records*.jsonl` (one atlas record a line). This puts them into the
coordinator's database. Every line is decoded with the wire contract's codec
before it is sent, so a line that is not a `Problem` or a `Node` stops the load
and names its file and line. Rows go up five hundred at a time as one JSON array
parameter, unpacked by PostgreSQL itself, and loading the same directory twice
changes nothing but what may change: a problem's status and a node's rank.
Stages, statements and trails are the factory's own and are never touched.

## Note
How many lines go up in one statement.

## To loadBatchSize () -> Int:
    Return 500.

## Note
The statements that place a batch, each reading the JSON array in `$1`.

## To problemInsertSql () -> Text:
    Let mutable q be ["INSERT INTO factory.problem (id, title, source, cohort, collection, category, statement_informal, lean_statement,"].
    Push "lean_module, lean_declaration, external_key, cross_ref, status) SELECT e->>'id', e->>'title', e->>'source', e->>'cohort'," to q.
    Push "e->>'collection', e->>'category', e->>'statementInformal', e->>'leanStatement', e->>'leanModule', e->>'leanDeclaration'," to q.
    Push "e->>'externalKey', e->>'crossRef', e->>'status' FROM jsonb_array_elements($1::jsonb) AS e" to q.
    Push "ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status" to q.
    Return join(q, " ").

## To nodeInsertSql () -> Text:
    Let mutable q be ["INSERT INTO factory.node (id, parent_id, kind, label, problem_id, stage, rank)"].
    Push "SELECT e->>'id', e->>'parentId', e->>'kind', e->>'label', e->>'problemId', e->>'stage', (e->>'rank')::int" to q.
    Push "FROM jsonb_array_elements($1::jsonb) AS e ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET rank = EXCLUDED.rank" to q.
    Return join(q, " ").

## To profileUpdateSql () -> Text:
    Return "UPDATE factory.problem p SET opdp = e->'p' FROM jsonb_array_elements($1::jsonb) AS e WHERE p.id = e->>'id'".

## To rankSyncSql () -> Text:
    Return "UPDATE factory.problem p SET rank = n.rank FROM factory.node n WHERE n.problem_id = p.id AND n.kind = 'problem' AND p.rank <> n.rank".

## Note
What one line sends, after it passes its file's check: a problem or a node as it
is, an atlas record as its profile keyed by the problem it profiles. Escaped NUL
characters are replaced first (`load_rules.lg`).

## To loadLine (kind: Text, raw: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Let line be withoutNul(raw).
    If kind is equal to "problems":
        Inspect fromJson_Problem(line):
            When Ok (p):
                Return a new Ok with value line.
            When Err (e):
                Return a new Err with error e.
    If kind is equal to "nodes":
        Inspect fromJson_Node(line):
            When Ok (n):
                Return a new Ok with value line.
            When Err (e):
                Return a new Err with error e.
    Inspect jsonParseStrict(line):
        When JOk (v):
            If opdpProblemId(v) is equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error "an atlas record without an integer problem_id".
            Return a new Ok with value "{{\"id\":" + jsonQuote(opdpProblemId(v)) + ",\"p\":" + opdpProfile(v) + "}}".
        When JErr (m):
            Return a new Err with error m.
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable line".

## Note
One batch sent as a JSON array: how many lines it carried.

## To sendBatch (c: PgConn, sql: Text, batch: Seq of Text) -> Result of Int and Text:
    If length of batch is equal to 0:
        Return a new Ok with value 0.
    Inspect pgQueryParams(c, sql, ["[" + join(batch, ",") + "]"]):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (qr):
            Return a new Ok with value (length of batch).
    Return a new Err with error "unsent".

## Note
Every line of a file sent with `sql` in batches. Answers how many lines went up.

## To loadLines (c: PgConn, path: Text, kind: Text, sql: Text) -> Result of Int and Text:
    Inspect read(path):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "cannot read {path}: " + e.
        When Ok (text):
            Let mutable batch be a new Seq of Text.
            Let mutable sent be 0.
            Let mutable lineNo be 0.
            Let all be lines(text).
            Let total be length of all.
            Repeat for line in all:
                Set lineNo to lineNo + 1.
                If trim(line) is not equal to "":
                    Inspect loadLine(kind, line):
                        When Err (e):
                            Return a new Err with error "{path}:{lineNo}: " + e.
                        When Ok (out):
                            Push out to batch.
                If length of batch is at least loadBatchSize() or lineNo is equal to total:
                    Inspect sendBatch(c, sql, batch):
                        When Err (e):
                            Return a new Err with error "{path} near line {lineNo}: " + e.
                        When Ok (n):
                            Set sent to sent + n.
                    Set batch to a new Seq of Text.
            Return a new Ok with value sent.
    Return a new Err with error "unread".
